.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt SET_MEMPOLICY 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm set_mempolicy
.Nd set the memory policy of the calling thread, on a machine of one memory node
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In numaif.h
.Ft long
.Fn set_mempolicy "int mode" "const unsigned long *nodemask" "unsigned long maxnode"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn set_mempolicy
gives the calling thread a NUMA memory policy and answers as Linux 6.12
answers on a machine with one memory node, node 0.
Every page comes from node 0 under every policy, so the policy changes no
allocation; it is checked, kept, and read back by
.Xr get_mempolicy 2 .
A child of
.Xr fork 2
and a new thread take the caller's policy, and
.Xr execve 2
keeps it.
libnuma, numactl and the Java runtime set one.
.Pp
.Fa mode
is one of
.Dv MPOL_DEFAULT
.Pq 0 ,
which leaves the thread without a policy,
.Dv MPOL_PREFERRED
.Pq 1 ,
.Dv MPOL_BIND
.Pq 2 ,
.Dv MPOL_INTERLEAVE
.Pq 3 ,
.Dv MPOL_LOCAL
.Pq 4 ,
.Dv MPOL_PREFERRED_MANY
.Pq 5
and
.Dv MPOL_WEIGHTED_INTERLEAVE
.Pq 6 ,
with any of the flags
.Dv MPOL_F_STATIC_NODES
.Pq 0x8000 ,
.Dv MPOL_F_RELATIVE_NODES
.Pq 0x4000
and
.Dv MPOL_F_NUMA_BALANCING
.Pq 0x2000
set in it.
.Dv MPOL_PREFERRED
with an empty mask is kept, and read back, as
.Dv MPOL_LOCAL .
.Pp
.Fa nodemask
has
.Fa maxnode No \- 1
bits, in longs.
A null
.Fa nodemask ,
and a
.Fa maxnode
of 0 or 1, is the empty mask.
The kernel knows 1024 nodes, as Debian's does; of a longer mask the part
past them is read a long at a time and must be zeros.
.Dv MPOL_DEFAULT
and
.Dv MPOL_LOCAL
take the empty mask alone.
Every other mode needs node 0 in its mask, the nodes the machine does not
have being dropped from it; under
.Dv MPOL_F_RELATIVE_NODES
any node will do, since the mask is folded onto the nodes the thread may
use, which is node 0.
A policy set with a flag reads back the mask the caller gave, and one
without a flag node 0.
.Ss System call interface
The system call number is 276 on i386 and 238 on x86-64.
On the x86-64 kernel a 32-bit program's mask is of 32-bit longs.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
0 on success.
On failure -1 is returned with
.Va errno
set; the kernel returns the negative error number.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Pa tests/numaprobe.c
sets each mode, reads it back, and passes it through
.Xr fork 2
and
.Xr execve 2 .
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width "[EFAULT]"
.It Bq Er EFAULT
.Fa nodemask
cannot be read.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fa mode
is none of the seven;
.Dv MPOL_F_STATIC_NODES
comes with
.Dv MPOL_F_RELATIVE_NODES ;
.Dv MPOL_F_NUMA_BALANCING
comes with a mode other than
.Dv MPOL_BIND
and
.Dv MPOL_PREFERRED_MANY ;
the mask has more bits than a page holds;
a bit past node 1023 is set;
.Dv MPOL_DEFAULT
or
.Dv MPOL_LOCAL
has a node in its mask;
.Dv MPOL_LOCAL ,
or
.Dv MPOL_PREFERRED
with an empty mask, has
.Dv MPOL_F_STATIC_NODES
or
.Dv MPOL_F_RELATIVE_NODES ;
or another mode has a mask that is empty or, without
.Dv MPOL_F_RELATIVE_NODES ,
leaves node 0 out.
.It Bq Er ENOMEM
There is no memory for the policy.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr get_mempolicy 2 ,
.Xr mbind 2 ,
.Xr move_pages 2
